i-center, randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind trial.\n\nPower calculation:\n\nThe assumption of sample size calculation:\n\ndifference 18% (8% : 26%) α: 0.05, statistical power: 90%, two sided difference: 18% Compliance: 80%\n\n\\- Unadjusted sample size (N=200) 180 + 10(%) drop out = 180 + 180/ (1-0.1)2 = 222.2 Total 220 subjects","testedNonInferiority":false,"nonInferiorityType":"SUPERIORITY_OR_OTHER","pValue":"<0.05","statisticalMethod":"Regression, Logistic","paramType":"Odds Ratio (OR)","paramValue":"0.84","ciPctValue":"95","ciNumSides":"TWO_SIDED","ciLowerLimit":"0.17","ciUpperLimit":"4.15","dispersionType":"STANDARD_ERROR_OF_MEAN","dispersionValue":"0.40"}]},{"type":"SECONDARY","title":"Presence of Bowel Habit Change (Watery Stools More Than 2 Times Per Day for at Least 2 Days)","reportingStatus":"POSTED","paramType":"NUMBER","unitOfMeasure":"participants","timeFrame":"Up to14 days","groups":[{"id":"OG000","title":"Lacidofil Capsule Versus Placebo Drug","description":"Lacidofil capsule: Lactobacillus rhamnosus R0011‧Lactobacillus acidophilus R0052 bacterial culture (2x109), maltodextrin, Mg stearate, ascorbic acid (1 capsule twice a day for 14 days) Placebo drug: maltodextrin, Mg stearate, ascorbic acid\n\n(1 capsule twice a day for 14 days)"}],"denoms":[{"units":"Participants","counts":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"214"}]}],"classes":[{"categories":[{"measurements":[{"groupId":"OG000","value":"25"}]}]}],"analyses":[{"groupIds":["OG000"],"groupDescription":"Null hypothesis: The efficay of the probiotic Lactobacilli (Lacidofil cap®) for the prevention of AAD in adults is not different form the placebo group in multi-center, randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind trial.\n\nPower calculation:\n\nThe assumption of sample size calculation:\n\ndifference 18% (8% : 26%) α: 0.05, statistical power: 90%, two sided difference: 18% Compliance: 80%\n\n\\- Unadjusted sample size (N=200) 180 + 10(%) drop out = 180 + 180/ (1-0.1)2 = 222.2 Total 220 subjects","